A schema that refers to another package of its module, which is invalid
however the lineage was loaded (ref-import): the lineage is the package that
declares it, and a package it imports is not part of it.
-- normal.cue --
import "example.com/fleet/common"

name: "ship"
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {name: common.#Name}
-- common/common.cue --
package common

#Name: string
-- out/verdict --
# bind
E0143 name in schema 0.0 refers to #Name, in package "example.com/fleet/common", which is not one of CUE's builtin packages
# ids
